# Attach contract — new ISA is not a copy of emit/llvm

File: oodac/docs/x86-codegen-style.oot

Product oodac emits LLVM IR and clang. That LLVM path is the reference, not a forever ban on other ISAs.

The LLVM reference gate is: four product mains `check`, product `build` of cli/ooda/opm, and llvm-self-host of `oodac/main.oo`. Concat of `oodac/main.oo` as the only compiler ELF is a fail (unique_fns host rebuild).

`--backend llvm` lives in `emit/llvm/` and consumes the typed artifact. Shared type names live in `types/`. Residual c/wasm/x86 stay exit 2. Kind drivers and landlock run on LLVM.

Do not restore `emit/c/` or `x86_emit_*.oo` as product.

Status: LLVM is the reference. A later ISA is a second consumer of the typed artifact.
